// Dannotalos, in his hall in the upper town at Bibracte: the house of
// Vettius's partner, who holds Brigodunon on his account. He receives the
// player as a thief (dannotalos_cheated), a partner (factor_turned), the
// house's man (house_factor) or a curiosity. He feeds strangers before he
// asks their business (Diodorus V.28), and eating makes the player his guest
// (dan_guest). Routes against him here: claim the champion's portion at the
// feast and beat Cingetos (a duel; the forfeit strikes the line); threaten
// him with Ateula's roll, or sell it to him; the Bone Field's iron (A2.4
// sets iron_tally); join him with the house's master book (the Pens are
// A2.5); or the knife. The night routes are at his chamber door
// (bib_chamber), the split at Cabillonum (cab_vettius), and interdiction
// with the druid (bib_druid).
=== start
[flag champion_beaten, !flag dan_forfeit] -> forfeit
[flag dan_duel, !flag champion_beaten, !flag dan_duel_done] -> duel_lost
[flag dan_met] -> again
~ set dan_met
[!quest partner done] ~ quest partner met
[quest brig_line none] ~ quest brig_line start
[quest house_vettius none] ~ quest house_vettius start
The hall is long and full of smoke and people: dogs under the tables, men on hides along the walls with their shields hung above them, a boy turning a whole pig on a spit over the hearth. In the middle of it all, on a bench by the fire with a tablet in his lap, sits an Aeduan not yet thirty, with a gold torc as thick as a child's wrist. He closes the tablet when he sees you.
[flag partners_split] -> met_split
[flag dannotalos_cheated] -> met_thief
[flag factor_turned] -> met_partner
[flag house_factor] -> met_factor
-> met_curious

=== met_curious
"A Cadurcan," he says. "There aren't so many in Bibracte this year that I can't guess which. Brigodunon." He smiles with half his mouth. "You're on my book. I'm Dannotalos."
-> custom

=== met_thief
"Brigodunon," he says, before you're halfway down the hall. "The Cadurcan who collected my property at Noviodunum, on my account, with my letter, and left me the other half to pay." He doesn't get up. "Orbius wrote to me. Romans always write. I'm Dannotalos." The half smile. "I've been looking forward to this."
-> custom

=== met_partner
"Partner," he says, and the men nearest the fire look round. "Epomeduos wrote you into my letter at Avaricum. He had no business to. He's a clever boy, and he likes making promises in my name." He considers you. "I'm Dannotalos. I keep my clever boys' promises when it suits me. Let's find out whether it does."
-> custom

=== met_factor
"The house's new factor for the Cadurci hills." He doesn't get up. "Vettius writes to me about everything. He's very pleased with you. He says you have a good hand." He turns the tablet over in his lap. "I'm Dannotalos. Vettius's partner, and so, I suppose, yours."
-> custom

=== met_split
He knows. You can see it from the door: he knows whose doing it was that the Roman closed his account. "Brigodunon," he says quietly. "You've cost me the Roman, and every line I ever sold him. I'm Dannotalos, since you've done me the honor of ruining me without being introduced."
-> custom

=== custom
"Eat first," he says. "Then tell me who you are and what you want, though I know both. That's the custom of this house, and of every house in Gaul worth the name. We don't ask a stranger his business on an empty belly."
* Sit down and eat. -> feast
* "I'll stand." -> hub

=== feast
~ set dan_guest; time 120; heal 5
They sit you on a wolfskin on the floor at a low table, among his men. He sits in the middle of the ring like the leader of a chorus, his guests by rank on either side of him; behind each warrior his shield-bearer stands with the shield, and across the floor his spearmen sit in a ring of their own. The meat comes off the spits in joints, and they eat it with both hands and cut what they can't tear with a little knife from the belt. A boy carries the cup round. There is one cup, and everyone drinks from it, a mouthful at a time, often.

The thigh joint, the best of the pig, goes by right to the big man with the broken nose at Dannotalos's right hand. Nobody watches it go, and everybody knows where it's going.

"Cingetos," Dannotalos says, seeing you see. "My champion. The champion's portion is his until somebody takes it off him. In my grandfather's day men died over that joint at the table." He drinks. "We're more civilized now. Now, then. Who are you, and what do you want?"
-> hub

