=== who
"Who am I." He likes the question. "My house is old. When I was fourteen it was also poor, and the Sequani had beaten us with the Germans' help, and the Aedui had to give them hostages: the sons of the best houses, and an oath that the city would never ask for them back." He turns the cup in his hands. "Nobody did. It took a Roman to remember us, after he'd beaten the Germans and wanted something to give the Aedui."

"So I know what a hostage is worth, and to whom, from the inside. There are a great many in Gaul this year. Somebody is going to own them when it's over. I'd rather it was somebody who knows what they are."
-> hub

=== brig
"Brigodunon is on my account," he agrees. "Every hearth, every head. The house paid me for it at a fair price, and I'll collect after the harvest, if there's anything left to collect." He holds up a hand. "Don't look at me like that. If it weren't on my book it would be on somebody's, and somebody's book is worse."

"Bring me a reason to strike it, and I'll listen. Reasons are the only thing I buy that I can't sell again."
-> hub

=== forward
"Because a war is a harvest, and the harvest is coming whether I buy it or not." He says it patiently, as a man explains rain. "On my book, people are property, and property is fed, and kept dry, and delivered in one piece. Off it, they're loot, and loot is whatever the man who caught it feels like. Ask any Roman's slave which he'd rather be."

"And the revolt," he adds, "since you're too polite to ask. Yes. I sell iron to the king's smiths. A long war is good for prices, and when it's over somebody will have to lead Gaul, and it had better be the Aedui." He smiles. "Meaning me."

"Losses in transit run about a tenth on my account. It's a long road from the Liger to the Arar."
[flag survivor_out] ~ set dan_transit
[flag survivor_out] You think of the girl at Avaricum, written down as Dannotalos's property, lost in transit, going into the reeds like a hare. A tenth is a great many girls.
-> hub

=== partner_offer
~ set dan_offer
He sets the cup down. For the first time he looks at you the way he looks at the tablet.

"Vettius has the book and the boats and the Roman coin. I have the people. Every year he takes more of the price and I take more of the risk." He spreads his hands. "Bring me his master book, and the trade is mine: a Gallic house, not a Roman one, and the partners on it are partners of mine. Or bring me the Pens, where he keeps his stock for the boats." He shrugs. "Either one, and Brigodunon is off every book there is. You'd be the one keeping it."
-> hub

=== join
He holds out his hand for it, and you don't give it to him yet, and he laughs.
"Good. You're learning. Well?"
* Give it to him. "Make me your partner." -> joined
* "Not yet." -> hub

=== joined
~ take master_book; set dan_partner; deed joined_house; honor -10; silver 100; xp 100
[!quest partner done] ~ quest partner done_partner done
~ quest house_vettius partner_joined
[!quest brig_line done] ~ quest brig_line done_partner done; set house_left; clear epo_at_brig
[quest house_collects active] ~ quest house_collects done_struck done
He takes the book onto his knees and opens it, and goes through it leaf by leaf for a long time with his lips moving, while the hall gets on with its dinner around him. When he finds Brigodunon he draws his thumbnail through the wax, deliberately, and shows you.

"Struck. Partners' villages are kept off the book." He closes it. "Vettius will hear by the end of the month. By then it won't matter what he hears." He hands you a purse. "Your share of the first quarter, in advance. Welcome to the house of Dannotalos."
-> hub

=== claim
The hall goes quiet in pieces, from the middle outward, like ice breaking. Cingetos stops chewing. Dannotalos looks at you, and then at his men, who are all looking at him.

"The champion's portion," he says, "in my hall." He doesn't sound angry. He sounds like a man doing sums. "It's an old custom. Very well. One on one, on the floor of my hall, and nobody helps either of you. It ends when one of you can't stand. Win, and the joint is yours, and I'll pay a forfeit worthy of my house."
[!quest brig_line done] "Brigodunon," you say. "Struck off your account." "Done," he says, quite pleasantly. "And if Cingetos wins, you've eaten my meat and lost my floor, and everyone in Bibracte will know it."
[quest brig_line done] "And the forfeit?" "Silver," he says. "As much as you weigh." The hall laughs. "And if Cingetos wins, you've eaten my meat and lost my floor, and everyone in Bibracte will know it."
* "Agreed." -> duel
* "On second thought, the joint is his." -> claim_back

=== claim_back
~ honor -2
There's laughter, and Cingetos goes back to his meat, and Dannotalos raises the cup to you as if you'd done something sensible. Perhaps you have.
-> hub

=== duel
~ set dan_duel; duel dan_champion champion_beaten
They drag the tables back to the walls. Cingetos wipes his hands on his trousers and takes his shield from the boy behind him, and stands in the firelight in the middle of the floor, and waits.

=== forfeit
~ set dan_forfeit; renown 3; xp 150; title Who took the champion's portion in Dannotalos's hall
