"The gods' iron." He says it softly, so the men at the next table don't hear. "Out of the Bone Field, through my agent, to the king's smiths. Sacrilege, the priests would call it. If they heard it from you, with a sworn man beside you, nobody in Gaul would speak to me again."

He calls for wax and writes the release, and seals it, and sends it to the Arar tonight. "Go to the priests anyway, if you like," he says. "But you'd be wasting a good threat on a bad man."
-> hub

=== draw
~ set dan_draw
[flag dan_guest] -> draw_guest
He sees it. So does everyone in the hall: his spearmen are on their feet before you've cleared the sheath.

"In my own hall," he says. "Well."
* Do it. -> kill
* Put the knife away. -> sheathe

=== draw_guest
You ate his meat. You drank from his cup. In this hall, and in any hall in Gaul, that makes the next thing worse than murder, and every man here knows it.

"Under my roof," Dannotalos says, "with my bread in you." He doesn't move. "Go on, then. They'll sing about it."
* Do it anyway. -> kill_guest
* Put the knife away. -> sheathe

=== sheathe
The spearmen sit down slowly. Nobody laughs. Dannotalos picks up his cup again, and the boy comes round with the meat, and everyone in the hall will remember this, including you.
-> hub

=== kill
~ fight
He's off the bench and behind the hearth before you're on him, quicker than you'd think, and his men come over the tables.

=== kill_guest
~ violate dannotalos; fight
He's off the bench and behind the hearth before you're on him, quicker than you'd think, and his men come over the tables.
